-- pending: refused #491
-- now: 16:1: `show__wasi_stdout_cell` loops, so it is called in direct style one step at a time, and a borrow at `'t` cannot stay open across its steps: it may take one borrow of a cell at `'t`, `imm 't A` or `mut 't A`, which it borrows again at each step (SPEC §14, borrow scopes over loops)
--
-- A counted `for` over a view parameter, in a function with a lifetime parameter whose body
-- performs an operation of `Stdout`. The function's copy for the platform's handler takes the
-- capability's cell as a parameter before the view (`show__wasi_stdout_cell`), so the view is not
-- among the parameters the elaboration types before deciding whether the body loops (`lentDef`):
-- the `for`'s source has no type, and the copy is taken to loop. With the `print_byte` moved out
-- of `show`, into `main`, the program is accepted.
--
-- Once it lands: `ab` then `i32[2]`, `live 0`.

include textio

-- The bytes of `l` written one at a time, and how many.
fn show<'t>(l: text 't) -> i32 =
  let mut k = 0;
  for p in l { print_byte(*p); k = k + 1 };
  k

main -> i32 =
  let s = string_of_lit("ab");
  let n = borrow imm s { 't, t -> show(t) };
  n
